let sitePanel = stack() {
	paragraph("A site is more than one page. You are reading pages/index.caja of {{.Name}}; the About link in the header goes to pages/about.caja. Both are ordinary modules that export a Page, and main.caja is a short loop that renders and writes each one.")
	paragraph("This tab spans both packages. Page and definePage come from @caja/ui — a page with a title, an output path and some content is universal, with nothing theme-specific to decide. siriguela owns the three below it, because how the chrome LOOKS is exactly what a theme is for.")
	paragraph("Neither package writes a file. Writing is the doc module's job and stays in main.caja on purpose: a library that wrote files would make every program importing it un-runnable with caja run.")
	componentDoc(
		"Page / definePage(title, path, content) — @caja/ui",
		"A Page is a title, an output path (also the href other pages use) and its content. Named arguments disambiguate the two adjacent strings — a typo swapping title and path is a String in the wrong String-typed slot, which no analyzer can catch positionally.",
		"let home = definePage(title: \"Home\", path: \"index.html\", content: homeContent)\nlet about = definePage(title: \"About\", path: \"about.html\", content: aboutContent)\n\nlet site: [Page] = [home, about]",
		codeSample("Page{title: \"Home\", path: \"index.html\", content: ...}")
	)
	componentDoc(
		"siteNav(pages, currentPath) — @caja/siriguela",
		"One link per page, with the current one marked aria-current='page' — an accessibility hint and the stylesheet's highlight hook. It is ui's navLinks with this theme's class on it, and renderPage puts it in every page's header for you.",
		"siteNav(site, \"about.html\")",
		siteNav([
			definePage(title: "Home", path: "index.html", content: paragraph("")),
			definePage(title: "About", path: "about.html", content: paragraph(""))
		], "about.html")
	)
	componentDoc(
		"renderPage(current, all, footerNote, stylesheetHref) — @caja/siriguela",
		"Everything between a Page and the file you write: the shared chrome (navigation, footer) wrapped in a complete HTML document, returned as a String. This is the only call main.caja needs per page.",
		"doc.write(\"dist/\${current.path}\", renderPage(current, site, \"A footer note.\", \"style.css\"))",
		codeSample("<!doctype html><html lang='en'>...")
	)
	componentDoc(
		"siteStylesheet() — @caja/siriguela",
		"The theme's entire CSS as a String: the base rules, the chrome, the CSS-only interactive components, the hover states, and the responsive block. Write it once and a project has no hand-written CSS at all.",
		"doc.write(\"dist/style.css\", siteStylesheet())",
		codeSample("*, *::before, *::after{box-sizing:border-box;}body{...")
	)
	subheading("How main.caja assembles the site")
	paragraph("A page list, a footer note and a recursive writer. Add a page module, import it, add it to the list — that is the entire workflow.")
	codeSample("import * from \"@caja/siriguela\"\nimport * from \"@caja/ui\"\nimport \"pages/index\" as home\nimport \"pages/about\" as about\n\nlet site: [Page] = [home.page, about.page]\n\nconst writeSite = fn(remaining: [Page], all: [Page]) -> Nothing {\n\tif (array.len(remaining) == 0) {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tlet current = array.head(remaining)\n\tdoc.write(\"dist/\${current.path}\", renderPage(current, all, footerNote, \"style.css\"))\n\treturn writeSite(array.tail(remaining), all)\n}\n\nwriteSite(site, site)\ndoc.write(\"dist/style.css\", siteStylesheet())")
}

